{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hadron-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:hadron-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of hadrons up to braid isotopy","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hadron-exists","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hecke-normal-form"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-hadron-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","hadron","isotopy"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Hadron.unique_up_to_isotopy","text":"hadron-unique.md","leanSource":"hadron-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:hadron-unique\"></a><p>Two hadrons sharing a crossing partition, localisation point <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>, and Hecke normal form coincide up to braid isotopy.</p>\n<p>The Hecke normal form furnishes a canonical representative. Thus, uniqueness denotes uniqueness of the Hecke class in the algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(R, q)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"9.3.5","page":"b/prop-hadron-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":89,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":69},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Hadron.unique_up_to_isotopy","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-unique.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
